      "content": "A source, approaching with speed u towards the open end of a stationary pipe of length L, is emitting a sound of frequency f<sub>s</sub>. The farther end of the pipe is closed. The speed of sound in air is v and f<sub>0</sub> is the fundamental frequency of the pipe. For which of the following combination(s) of u and f<sub>s</sub>, will the sound reaching the pipe lead to a resonance?",
      "options": [
        {
          "identifier": "A",
          "content": "u = 0.8v and f<sub>s</sub> = f<sub>0</sub>"
        },
        {
          "identifier": "B",
          "content": "u = 0.8v and f<sub>s</sub> = 2f<sub>0</sub>"
        },
        {
          "identifier": "C",
          "content": "u = 0.8v and f<sub>s</sub> = 0.5f<sub>0</sub>"
        },
        {
          "identifier": "D",
          "content": "u = 0.5v and f<sub>s</sub> = 1.5f<sub>0</sub>"
        }
      ],
      "correct_options": [
        "A",
        "D"
      ],
